From: Tianyu9748 <54686548+Tianyu9748@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:38:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 16/26] [Diffusion] Causal KV seam: layer-overlapped restore
 (PROTOTYPE, not for reelcache-integration)

Prototype for measuring a layer-overlapped restore of archived session KV; not merged into
the integration branch the ReelCache freezes pin.

- CausalSelfAttentionKVCache.restore_pending (default None: unchanged): a backend that installs
  restored history in the background leaves a per-layer readiness object there. The first K/V
  access, at the top of update_and_get_attention_kv, waits on it once, before the eviction roll
  can move restored tokens. can_direct_current_attention is False while a restore is pending.
- Session handle key overlap_restore (off | first_forward | early) selects the mode per request.
- Early restore: the GPU worker offers each causal stage's begin_causal_kv_early_restore at
  dispatch, before text encoding and latent preparation, in inference mode. The stage hands its
  existing caches and RoPE to the backend's early_restore. The worker calls the backend's
  release_early_restore once the request returned or failed. Best effort: never fails a request.
- Unit tests: test_causal_kv_overlap.py (wait before writes and the roll, one-shot, typed failure,
  handle validation, the stage's early offer).

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
